statement:
Consider every array `nums` of length `n` that meets all of these rules:

- every entry is a positive integer (at least 1);
- any two neighbouring entries differ by at most 1;
- the entries add up to at most `maxSum`.

Return the largest value that `nums[index]` can have in such an array. Because `n <= maxSum`, the array of all ones always qualifies, so an answer exists.

validator:
function validate([n, index, maxSum]) {
  if (![n, index, maxSum].every(Number.isInteger)) return 'n, index and maxSum must be whole numbers.';
  if (n < 1) return 'n must be at least 1.';
  if (maxSum < n || maxSum > 1e9) return 'maxSum must be between n and 10^9.';
  if (index < 0 || index >= n) return 'index must be between 0 and n - 1.';
  return null;
}

